 open Senate seat sits in territory that has favored Republicans by double digits in recent cycles, and Republican Julia Letlow enters the final stretch as the clear favorite. She has raised roughly three times as much as Democrat Jamie Davis, and outside groups have put more than $11 million into the contest on each side, a level of spending that signals a genuinely contested race but not an upset in the making. Every major race rating places the seat in the Solid or Safe Republican column, and prediction markets give Davis roughly a one-in-fifteen chance.\n\nThe main wrinkle is polling. Only two surveys, both from Democratic-leaning sponsors, have tested the matchup, and each showed Letlow ahead by about four points, closer than raters expect. With thin, older, and partisan-sponsored polling, uncertainty remains elevated, but the fundamentals still point to a Republican hold.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0491, "margin": -9.91}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0664, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0312, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0328, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0575, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0895, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0752, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0962, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1593, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0833, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0984, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1142, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0801, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0669, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0515, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0698, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0644, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0666, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0772, "margin": -8.0}, {"date":